[section=getting-started][section_title1]Getting Started[/section_title1]
Head over to [url=https://github.com/ghsoares/Godot-RmlUi/releases]GitHub releases[/url] to download the latest version, extract and add [code]addons/[/code] folder to your project's main folder.

Enable it on project's Plugins settings and RmlUi is installed!

To start using it, add a [class RMLDocument] to your scene, it's a Control-based node, so feel free to adjust it's dimensions.
To make it show something, you need a [code].rml[/code] file and attach a script to load the file. 

Here's a sample document file:

[codeblocks]
[html=res://test.rml]
<rml>
<head>
	<style>
		body {
			display: flex;
			flex-direction: column;
			align-items: center;
			justify-content: center;
			gap: 4px;
		}
	</style>
</head>
<body>
	<h1>Hello!</h1>
	<button>Test Button</button>
	<svg src="icon.svg"/>
	<input type="text"/>
</body>
</rml>
[/html]
[/codeblocks]
And a script of courtesy:

[codeblocks]
[gdscript=res://test.gd]
extends RMLDocument

func _ready() -> void:
	load_from_path("res://test.rml")
[/gdscript]
[/codeblocks]
Attaching [code]res://test.gd[/code] to the [class RMLDocument] node and running the scene should show something like this:

[img=100%]$BASE_URL/resources/images/getting_started1.png[/img]
[/section][section=rmlui-api][section_title2]RmlUi API[/section_title2]
This GDExtension was created with [url=https://github.com/mikke89/RmlUi]RmlUi[/url], some of it's API is translated to GDExtension, like querying elements, setting attributes, properties, classes, etc.

Some of it's features are incompatible with this GDExtension, like for example:
[ul]
[*][url=https://mikke89.github.io/RmlUiDoc/pages/data_bindings.html]Data binding (model-view-controller)[/url], as it doesn't have support of adding data binding on runtime (RmlUi expects data bindings before even loading an document);
[*][url=https://mikke89.github.io/RmlUiDoc/pages/lua_manual.html]Lua[/url], as for scripting is recommended to use GDScript instead.
[/ul]
More features could be found incompatible with this GDExtension, if you find any issue, please report it to [url=https://github.com/ghsoares/Godot-RmlUi/issues]github issues[/url].
[/section]